(a) The engineering and environmental services division shall have the power to administer and enforce all regulations and procedures adopted to implement this division, including the right to maintain an action or procedure in any court of competent jurisdiction to compel compliance with or restrain any violation of this division.
(b) The engineering and environmental services division may:
(1) Administer, coordinate and oversee acquisition, design, construction and operation and maintenance (O&M) of municipal stormwater facilities and conveyances;
(2) Establish or oversee the establishment of development standards and guidelines;
(3) Determine the manner in which stormwater facilities should be operated;
(4) Inspect private systems which discharge to the MS4;
(5) Advise the county board of commissioners and other county departments on issues related to stormwater;
(6) Protect facilities and properties controlled by the county and to prescribe how such facilities and properties are used by others;
(7) Require facilities or activities that create new, increased or significantly changed stormwater contributions to comply with the terms of this division;
(8) Develop programs or procedures to control the discharge of pollutants to the MS4;
(9) Adopt and implement the stormwater management program for the county; and
(10) Require facilities or activities that create stormwater contributions which result in a noncompliance of the county MS4 NPDES permit, to initiate corrective action to achieve compliance.
(Ord. No. 00-5, § 2-6.1-155, 6-20-2000)

